    "notes": [
      "The counters record application-level Qt calls in ScanEngine only, not OS syscalls or NEXIS network requests.",
      "Final files include all physical/stamp fields, all evidence observations/coverage/read states/selected values and complete source receipts, including unknown/false/zero values. Raw graph hashes preserve all declared semantic fields and original ranges/bytes/native framing; allocation capacity and pointer addresses are deliberately excluded.",
      "Each mode runs in a fresh process with QT_HASH_SEED=0 and the same roots. Hash-map field keys are sorted for serialization; vector/recorded order is preserved.",
      "Pre/post os.stat stamps cover all 2,425 source candidates and six media folders using path/device/inode/size/mtime_ns. These checks occur outside the instrumented scan body.",
      "The direct temporary ScanEngine TU satisfies the archive symbols before archive extraction, so the original scanengine object is not linked. All other Canon objects use matching before/after archives.",
      "No production or test files were edited by this diagnostic. Instrumented scan time/memory are supplementary; uninstrumented application trials are run separately by root.",
      "The proof covers this real mounted corpus. Alias, cancellation, directory changes and database/file freshness also rely on the separately executed production regression tests, not a claim of NEXIS coverage."
    ]
